# Cuts
10mm/s, 50%, 3.7mm 
wasn't enough to get all the way through 2mm holes. I could punch them out, but a little slower or more power would be better.
3.5 mm holes seemed to be okay
5mm/s was fine


A kerf of .125 was just slightly too tight for the anchor. I was able to file it down to get it to fit. The same kerf was too loose for the box

The sheet thickness varies from 5.4-5.8mm

Changed inner slot kerf from -.125 to -.1 to make the slot wider
This was perfect for a 5.4mm anchor

Changed outer cut kerf from .125 to .15
about right for the outside. The wall-to-wall joints were a little loose, but the wall-to-base joints were perfect
loose wall joints are probably okay because they will be held in place by the tension


